    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1644">

                <pb facs="1189" n="1073" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1073"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 704.6712/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé d’Affaires of
                        Turkey</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 7th ultimo, in which you request, on behalf of your
                    Government, that, in the absence of diplomatic or consular representation of the
                    Ottoman Government in Mexico, the interests of Ottoman subjects residing in that
                    country may be placed in the hands of the officers of the United States
                    there.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to inform you that it has given this Government pleasure to
                    instruct its officers in Mexico to use their unofficial good offices in behalf
                    of Ottoman subjects who may require them, in accordance with the principles set
                    forth in Paragraph 174 of the Consular Regulations of the United States,<anchor
                        n="5" xml:id="d1644-f1"/> a copy of which I have the honor to enclose
                    herewith.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1644-f1" n="5" xml:id="d1644-f1-content">
                <p>See the text in the memorandum of May 7, <ref target="#pg1077">p. 1077</ref>.</p>
